            <ArticleTitle>Lack of value of procalcitonin for prediction of coronary aneurysms in Kawasaki disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>179-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We studied the clinical, biologic (white blood cells, C-reactive protein and procalcitonin) and echocardiographic findings in 18 children hospitalized for Kawasaki disease from January 1999 until February 2006 to determine if procalcitonin is a useful marker to predict coronary aneurysms. In our study, contrary to earlier reports, elevated procalcitonin was not correlated with development of coronary aneurysms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
